{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-certification coherence remediation: clarified that `final-push-rejected` is a scenario through the single shared retries-exhausted terminal branch after five clean merges, not a second branch or redundant test. The AC now requires one test per actual control-flow branch plus the five-clean-merge terminal scenario, preserving the exactly-one-final-push invariant."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786147130775232001,"uuid":"7326dc0a-1366-4319-ac04-e268f17cfa4d"}